    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "I see myself trying to go to the last argument very often. I know the `goto_right`, and I can use a (Argument), but I wonder if there is an easier way:\r\n- Go to last argument\r\n  - Paste\r\n\r\nOr\r\n- Change around last argument\r\n  - Insert mode after the last argument [from  `| fn (a,b,c)` to `fn (a,b,c|)`]",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I see myself trying to go to the last argument very often. I know the <code class=\"notranslate\">goto_right</code>, and I can use a (Argument), but I wonder if there is an easier way:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Go to last argument\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Paste</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Or</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Change around last argument\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Insert mode after the last argument [from  <code class=\"notranslate\">| fn (a,b,c)</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">fn (a,b,c|)</code>]</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
    "bodyText": "I see myself trying to go to the last argument very often. I know the goto_right, and I can use a (Argument), but I wonder if there is an easier way:\n\nGo to last argument\n\nPaste\n\n\n\nOr\n\nChange around last argument\n\nInsert mode after the last argument [from  | fn (a,b,c) to fn (a,b,c|)]",
